    {
        "id": 11,
        "name": "Arah-Aka [Sun Blessed Sands]",
        "mtype": "racial",
        "description":"The culture of Arah-Aka, known as the 'Sun Blessed Sands,' is predominantly made up of the Arah-Ka people, whose lives are shaped by the Scarlet Dunes and the volcanic heat of Mount Akora. Renowned for their artistry in glassmaking, they create intricate tools and ceremonial weapons, avoiding blades in favor of bludgeoning arms to honor a tradition of sparing harm to one another. Their society thrives on solar reverence, crafting rituals and knowledge around the sun's power, which they see as both a life-giver and a trial to overcome. Communal harmony and adaptability are central to their way of life, ensuring survival in a land where endurance is key. Through their mastery of craft, magic, and resilience, the Arah-Aka embody a deep connection to the unforgiving beauty of their desert home.",
        "ruleset": 0
    },
